                      (    forth6809.asm):06902         ; (confirmed separately to take a full 65536-iteration
                      (    forth6809.asm):06903         ; wraparound, not tested here - see TSTDOLP's own notes). This
                      (    forth6809.asm):06904         ; case IS fast and safe to test directly: QDOSETUP's own skip
                      (    forth6809.asm):06905         ; check happens before the loop is entered at all, confirmed by
                      (    forth6809.asm):06906         ; hand-trace of its code. Same "?DO I + LOOP" body, but since
                      (    forth6809.asm):06907         ; the body never runs, the seed should come back completely
                      (    forth6809.asm):06908         ; unchanged (0, not 10).
