                      (    forth6809.asm):09401                                   ; snapshot (MKDP/MKCODE/MKVAR/MKLATEST) is
                      (    forth6809.asm):09402                                   ; taken at its very start, before HEADER or
                      (    forth6809.asm):09403                                   ; any compiling runs at all - so DOMARKER
                      (    forth6809.asm):09404                                   ; correctly restores to the state BEFORE the
                      (    forth6809.asm):09405                                   ; marker word itself was created (TSTCBUF
                      (    forth6809.asm):09406                                   ; directly), not the state right after. The
                      (    forth6809.asm):09407                                   ; real dictionary/compile mechanism was
                      (    forth6809.asm):09408                                   ; already working correctly; only this
                      (    forth6809.asm):09409                                   ; test's own comparison target was wrong.
                      (    forth6809.asm):09410                    BNE  MKFAIL
